// Every pending `defer` runs before the panic ends the program, innermost scope
// first and last-registered first within a scope.
//
// Four handlers across three nesting levels: the two registered in the
// innermost block fire in reverse registration order, then the middle block's,
// then `main`'s. The panic is in the same function as all four, which is the
// part of unwinding that is implemented today: the generated fault block runs
// the *panicking function's* open scopes' defers before calling the runtime.
//
// A deferred `println` is the observable proof. Nothing here allocates, so
// there is no ownership question -- this program is about ordering only, and
// the expected stdout is its whole assertion.
fn main() {
    defer {
        println("outer");
    }

    if true {
        defer {
            println("middle 1");
        }

        if true {
            defer {
                println("middle 2");
            }
            defer {
                println("inner");
            }
            panic("cleanup");
        }
    }
}
